                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]InfiniPicross[/b] is nothing more than a random picross generator application. Or should I say, a white noise picross generator, because there isn't a single actual [i]picture[/i] in the game, outside of one achievement. It does what it's advertised to do, make entirely random puzzles, but beyond that, you'll be hard pressed to find much else to do with this game.\n\n[h1]Pros[/h1]\n[list][*]True to its name, can create whatever size puzzle your resolution supports in endless supply\n[*]Supports themes to customize the puzzle display and interface to your liking\n[*]It's cheap\n[*]Has achievements that require real effort, if you like a challenge[/list]\n\n[h1]Cons[/h1]\n[list][*]No campaign mode. No preset puzzles. No pictures. Isn't picross about pictures?\n[*]Has workshop support for custom themes, ok, but you can't upload or create custom puzzles. Why?\n[*]A resource hog. Slow startup, even slower puzzle generation. Really needs better optimization.\n[*]NO undo feature. You better not make mistakes!\n[*]One music track that gets old fast. I had to mute it.\n[*]This is a big one: It only supports puzzles as big as your maximum resolution. This means some people may find it impossible to complete the larger achievement requirements, the largest being 50x99. You're out of luck on old monitors.[/list]\n\nFrankly speaking, there are much better picross games, even free ones, on steam. And I sincerely mean no offense to the devs - you have made a solid random generator here. But getting personal, I enjoy picross for unveiling shapes and figures, not the pure logic aspect. As it is, this feels like a game for engineers and mathematicians.\n\nGrab it on sale if you grab it at all, and do your homework to be sure your PC can handle it, if achievements are your thing.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1505364779,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1505364802,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 52,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.843103289604187,
                        "comment_count": 2,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Well, sorry it took us so long to address your concerns, but I'd like to direct you towards InfiniPicross 2.0.\n-It has pictures.\n-Will soon get workshop support for pictures (working out how to make it simple).\n-Infinite amounts of undo.\n-Ambience system with multiple loops rather than a single, repetitive track.\n-Shader based display, so ridiculously fast display of huge puzzles with zooming functions and line hints at the corner.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1529354349,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
